# Exclude large app bundles (exceed GitHub 100MB file limit)
tom/darwin-arm64/MarkText.app/

# Retired tools — never commit their binaries. `d4rt` lost its source project
# (tom_d4rt_tool) on 2026-02-25; `dcli` carries the interpreter. A stray build
# left in the tree was swept in by tom_push_binaries' `git add -A` (c1e859d),
# so the ignore is what keeps a refresh from bringing it back.
tom/*/d4rt
tom/*/d4rt.exe

# Removed when the repository became public (2026-11-09) and kept out: core_bs
# (its source project is gone), test_bot and d4rtrun.b (example/test builds),
# dart_editor_bundler (tom_forge, private, BSD 3-Clause - allowed by the rule
# below, but nothing distributes it: run it from source with `dart run`).
# What may go in (DP-204 (c), 2026-11-12): a binary may go in when its licence is not copyleft - BSD, MIT, Apache and the like,
# licences that require no source to be published and bind nothing the binary is combined with
# - whether its source repository is public or private; GPL and other copyleft binaries stay out.
# Every binary here has a row in LICENSE (package, source repository, licence).
tom/*/core_bs
tom/*/core_bs.exe
tom/*/test_bot
tom/*/test_bot.exe
tom/*/d4rtrun.b
tom/*/d4rtrun.b.exe
tom/*/dart_editor_bundler
tom/*/dart_editor_bundler.exe
